  "schema": "training-session-mechanics",
  "authority": "Exact-person deliberate-training attribute stimulus and sustainable standing-training recovery. Skill EDU remains owned by training.json; aggregate cohort role stimulus remains owned by recruitment-cohort-profiles.json.",
  "standing_recovery": {
    "fatigue_recovery_per_24h": 8.0,
    "excess_deliberate_training_fatigue_per_hour": 0.5,
    "rule": "Standing training represents a distributed daily schedule with ordinary sleep and recovery. Training at or below the normal deliberate-hours ceiling creates no chronic fatigue by itself; elapsed full-day recovery removes saved fatigue. Only deliberate hours above the normal weekly ceiling create residual training fatigue. Immediate training, marching, combat, deprivation, wounds and other acute sources remain separate mechanics."
